  "text": "The city breathes in neon’s pale light,\nWhere shadows stretch and footsteps bite\nThe pavement’s cold and hollow chest,\nA solitary, silent guest.\n\nThrough crowds that drift like phantoms by,\nWith eyes cast down, they pass him by,\nLost in their own deep, private seas,\nUnseen, unheard, and unchained, free.\n\nYet in this tide of flesh and stone,\nHe stands alone, entirely alone,\nA void amidst the moving mass,\nWatching the urban hours pass.\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the giraffe."
